{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790970231,"nonce":"A5HQO8CnB8FGaxL+mt+tAoJyKwk=","title":"Null values pass static type checks: isOfType folds to true and typed catches take null","message":"Row: Issue7115.\n\n- ir/mir/expr/casts.rs `lower_type_check` folds a same-type check (same primitive, same class\n  or subclass) to `const true` with no null test (its comment says \"null check needed for refs\"),\n  so `Std.isOfType(nullString, String)` is true; a type-param source whose box fails also falls\n  back to true.\n- `throw` records the STATIC type id (stmt/statements.rs `runtime_type_id(expr.ty)`) and typed\n  catches compare ids with no null check, so a null String/Option/interface is caught by its typed\n  clause (Haxe: falls to the Dynamic one).","files":null}]}